    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0324" n="310" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg310"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/15240a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-17T20:00:00-04:00">January 17, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>85. I. In response to a New Year’s greeting sent by the Secretary of the
                        Navy,<anchor n="24" xml:id="d258-f1"/> the Navy Department has received,
                    presumably from the Naval Attaché,<anchor n="25" xml:id="d258-f2"/> a message
                    reading substantially as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The Secretary’s message has given Dr. T. V. Soong much gratification. Dr.
                            Soong is pleased to state that Generalissimo is coming to realize that
                            Soong’s differences of opinion are based on China’s welfare and that the
                            tension between Soong and the Generalissimo is greatly relaxed.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>II. We would be interested in your comments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d258-f1" n="24" xml:id="d258-f1-content">
